== run 1: deployctl
exit: 2
Usage: deployctl [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Deploy services and manage their configuration.

  Every command talks to the deploy API of the chosen environment.

Options:
  --config FILE             Read option defaults from an INI file.
  -v, --verbose             Say more; repeat for even more.
  --env [dev|staging|prod]  Target environment.  [env var: DEPLOYCTL_ENV;
                            default: dev]
  --version                 Show the version and exit.
  -h, --help                Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  config    Read and change remote configuration.
  logs      Show recent log lines of SERVICES.
  promote   Promote SERVICE from staging to prod. (DEPRECATED: Use 'release'
            instead.)
  release   Release VERSION of SERVICE.
  rollback  Roll SERVICE back to an earlier release.
  scale     Change how SERVICE scales.
  status    Show what runs where.
  sync      Copy service DIRS to the deploy host.
  user      Manage deploy users.
